{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3169","artifact_type":"architect","name":"plan/architect-duplicate-detection-content-match.md@sha256:58c84432012d62d67edaccf8ee45c1ad661d845a4c5e5f958254ddf710ff5759"},"owner_reference":"3169","content":"# Architecture Spec \u2014 Content-Based Duplicate Detection (#3169)\n\n**Scope**: WHAT to build \u2014 interfaces, contracts, data models, module boundaries.\nNo function bodies. Implementation belongs to `python-cli-architect` /\n`python-pytest-architect`.\n\n**Note on template fit**: This is a brownfield fix inside an existing package\n(`backlog_core`, `sam_schema`), not a new CLI tool. The greenfield sections of\n`architecture-spec-patterns.md` (PEP 723 distribution, new `cli/core/services/utils`\nlayout, Pydantic-settings config loading) do not apply and are omitted. Only the\nparts that generalize \u2014 type-domain patterns, error-hierarchy conventions, review\ncompliance, testing stack \u2014 are carried over and mapped onto the existing module\nlayout.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nDuplicate detection currently answers the wrong question, at the wrong time, in a\nform nobody can act on, using data that might already be stale \u2014 and it can only be\nreached from one of the two interfaces that are documented as equivalent. This spec\ncloses all five gaps with one shared primitive, not five unrelated patches:\n\n1. **Wrong match target** \u2192 Extract the full-text search engine already embedded in\n   `backlog_core/server.py` into a standalone, FastMCP-free module,\n   `backlog_core/search.py`. Add one new ranking function,\n   `find_content_duplicates()`, built on the same tokenizer/predicate engine.\n   `operations.py` and `server.py` both call the same functions \u2014 no second\n   algorithm.\n2. **Wrong timing** \u2192 `add_item()` keeps its unconditional write-time gate (now\n   content-based). The pre-write advisory check called out in\n   `create/start.md` Step 3 already exists and is unchanged\n   (`backlog_list(search=..., match_context=true)`); its CLI blind spot is closed\n   by item 5, not by inventing a second gate.\n3. **Unactionable result** \u2192 `DuplicateItemError` is redefined to carry a\n   `list[ContentDuplicateMatch]` \u2014 item reference, matched field, snippet \u2014 instead\n   of `(title, ratio, file_path)` tuples. Breaking change to `TestDuplicateItemError`,\n   confirmed expected.\n4. **Cache-only read reporting absence as fact** \u2192 The write-time gate becomes\n   tri-state internally (`DUPLICATE_FOUND` / `NO_DUPLICATE` / `COULD_NOT_VERIFY`).\n   When the active backend composes a cache from a remote provider\n   (`SyncProvider`) and no local match is found, one bounded incremental refresh\n   runs before the gate concludes \"no duplicate\" \u2014 paying the network cost only on\n   the path that is about to say it is safe to proceed, never on the path that\n   already found a match. If that refresh cannot complete, the item is still\n   created (AC5: no new rejections) but a warning is attached, through the\n   `Output` channel both interfaces already surface.\n5. **CLI has no `--search`** \u2192 Add `--search` to CLI `backlog list`, mirroring the\n   existing `merged-prs --search` idiom, wired to a new `search` parameter on\n   `operations.list_items()`.\n\nNo new dependency, no new backend-protocol member, no new CLI subcommand, no\nsemantic/embedding search. The existing token/boolean search engine is the\ncontent-matching primitive; literature on short-text duplicate detection backs\ntoken-overlap matching for this class of problem over character edit-distance\n(see \u00a711, ADR-004).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture Overview\n\n### 2.1 Context\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    Agent[\"Agent / user\"]\n    MCP[\"MCP: backlog_add / backlog_list\"]\n    CLI[\"CLI: backlog add / backlog list\"]\n    OPS[\"backlog_core/operations.py\"]\n    SEARCH[\"backlog_core/search.py (NEW)\"]\n    BACKEND[\"Configured backend\\n(GitHub / SQLite / Memory / Beads)\"]\n\n    Agent --> MCP\n    Agent --> CLI\n    MCP --> OPS\n    CLI --> OPS\n    MCP -.match_context enrichment.-> SEARCH\n    OPS --> SEARCH\n    OPS --> BACKEND\n```\n\n### 2.2 Container \u2014 where the shared primitive sits\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n    subgraph server.py [server.py \u2014 FastMCP, existing]\n        BL[\"backlog_list()\"]\n        BA[\"backlog_add()\"]\n        MC[\"match-context annotation\\n(_parse_body_sections, _make_snippet_parts,\\n_format_match_text \u2014 UNCHANGED, stay here)\"]\n    end\n    subgraph search_py [search.py \u2014 NEW, no FastMCP import]\n        TOK[\"tokenize_search()\"]\n        FILT[\"apply_search_filter()\"]\n        PRED[\"_Predicate / _SearchParser family\\n(moved verbatim from server.py)\"]\n        FIND[\"find_content_duplicates()\\n(NEW)\"]\n    end\n    subgraph operations_py [operations.py \u2014 existing]\n        LI[\"list_items(search=...) NEW param\"]\n        AI[\"add_item()\"]\n        CFD[\"_check_for_duplicates()\\nUPDATED\"]\n    end\n    subgraph cli [sam_schema/backlog.py \u2014 existing]\n        CLIST[\"list_items() +--search NEW\"]\n        CADD[\"add()\"]\n    end\n\n    BL --> FILT\n    BL --> MC\n    LI --> FILT\n    CFD --> FIND\n    FIND --> FILT\n    FIND --> TOK\n    AI --> CFD\n    CADD --> AI\n    CLIST --> LI\n```\n\n`search.py` has zero dependency on `fastmcp`/`mcp` types \u2014 it operates on\n`list[dict[str, str | bool]]`, the exact shape `operations.py::_build_list_entry`\nalready produces. This is what makes it importable from both `operations.py`\n(no FastMCP) and `server.py` (FastMCP) without a layering violation.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technology Stack\n\nNo new runtime dependency. Reused, already-present:\n\n- `difflib` \u2014 removed from the duplicate-detection path (see ADR-004); no longer\n  imported by `operations.py` for this purpose.\n- Existing tokenizer/recursive-descent parser (`_tokenize_search`, `_SearchParser`)\n  \u2014 relocated, not rewritten.\n- `dataclasses` (stdlib) \u2014 `ContentDuplicateMatch`.\n- `enum.StrEnum` (stdlib, Python 3.11+) \u2014 `DuplicateCheckStatus`.\n- `typer` `Annotated` option syntax \u2014 for the new CLI `--search` flag, mirroring\n  the existing `merged-prs --search` option verbatim.\n- Test stack unchanged: `pytest`, `pytest-mock` (`MockerFixture`), no `unittest.mock`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Component Design\n\n### 4.1 `backlog_core/search.py` (NEW MODULE)\n\n**Purpose**: the one content-matching primitive both `operations.py` and\n`server.py` call. Pure functions and dataclasses over\n`list[dict[str, str | bool]]` \u2014 no I/O, no backend access, no FastMCP import.\n\n**Moved here verbatim from `backlog_core/server.py`** (behavior unchanged; this\nis a relocation, not a rewrite \u2014 `server.py` imports them back):\n\n- `_tokenize_search` \u2192 public `tokenize_search(query: str) -> list[str]`\n- `_SearchParser`, `_Predicate`, `_TermPred`, `_AndPred`, `_OrPred`, `_NotPred`,\n  `_TruePred` (stay private to the module \u2014 internal AST, no external caller\n  needs them)\n- `_apply_search_filter` \u2192 public\n  `apply_search_filter(items: list[dict[str, str | bool]], query: str) -> list[dict[str, str | bool]]`\n- `_build_haystack`, `_item_matches_term`, `_SEARCH_FIELDS` (stay private)\n- `_parse_body_sections`, `_make_snippet`, `_make_snippet_parts`,\n  `_format_match_text`, `_META_FIELDS`, `_SNIPPET_WINDOW`,\n  `_DEFAULT_SNIPPET_CONTEXT` (stay private; `server.py`'s `match_context`\n  formatting keeps calling them, now via `from backlog_core.search import ...`)\n\n`server.py` deletes its copies and imports from `backlog_core.search`. This is\nthe concrete fix for problem 1: one algorithm, two callers.\n\n**New in this module**:\n\n```python\nclass DuplicateCheckStatus(StrEnum):\n    \"\"\"Outcome of a content-based duplicate check. See Type Contract in \u00a76.\"\"\"\n    DUPLICATE_FOUND = \"duplicate_found\"\n    NO_DUPLICATE = \"no_duplicate\"\n    COULD_NOT_VERIFY = \"could_not_verify\"\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass ContentDuplicateMatch:\n    \"\"\"One candidate duplicate, carrying enough for a caller to act on it.\"\"\"\n    title: str\n    item_ref: str          # \"#3141\" or \"bd-a3f8\" \u2014 never a bare file path\n    matched_field: str      # e.g. \"title\", \"body:acceptance-criteria\"\n    snippet: str            # ~120-char window around the match, via _make_snippet_parts\n    match_count: int        # number of concept-query terms this candidate matched\n\n\ndef build_concept_query(title: str, description: str, *, max_concepts: int = 4) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Build an OR query from significant words in title + description.\n\n    Mirrors the concept-extraction create/start.md Step 3 already prescribes\n    manually (\"extract 2 to 4 key concepts ... build {c1} OR {c2} OR {c3}\") \u2014\n    this makes that step's logic reusable instead of re-derived ad hoc by every\n    caller. Drops a small embedded stopword set and tokens under a minimum\n    length; returns \"\" when no usable concept remains (caller treats \"\" as\n    \"nothing to check against\").\n    \"\"\"\n    ...\n\n\ndef find_content_duplicates(\n    title: str,\n    description: str,\n    candidates: list[dict[str, str | bool]],\n    *,\n    max_results: int = 5,\n) -> list[ContentDuplicateMatch]:\n    \"\"\"Rank existing items whose content overlaps the new item's concept query.\n\n    Builds the query via build_concept_query, filters candidates via\n    apply_search_filter, ranks by number of matched terms (descending), and\n    projects the top max_results into ContentDuplicateMatch \u2014 reusing\n    _make_snippet_parts for the snippet field. Returns [] when the query is\n    empty or nothing matches.\n    \"\"\"\n    ...\n```\n\n### 4.2 `backlog_core/operations.py` (MODIFIED)\n\n- **`_classify_duplicate_check`** (NEW, private) \u2014 the actual tri-state\n  decision, split out so `DuplicateCheckStatus` has one real construction\n  site instead of being implicit in control flow:\n\n  ```python\n  def _classify_duplicate_check(\n      title: str, description: str, repo: str, out: Output\n  ) -> tuple[DuplicateCheckStatus, list[ContentDuplicateMatch]]:\n      \"\"\"Classify title/description against existing items; never raises for\n      DUPLICATE_FOUND or COULD_NOT_VERIFY \u2014 the caller decides what to do.\n\n      Reads the local cache via _build_list_entry(item, {}) over\n      backend.list_work_items() and scores it with find_content_duplicates().\n      If nothing matches and the backend is a SyncProvider, performs one\n      bounded incremental refresh (refresh_local_cache_from_github(repo=repo,\n      output=out), full_refresh=False) and re-scores once. A refresh failure\n      \u2014 caught as (GithubException, BacklogError), the same tuple\n      _try_create_github_issue already catches in this file \u2014 appends a\n      warning to out and yields COULD_NOT_VERIFY rather than propagating.\n      \"\"\"\n      ...\n  ```\n\n  Decision table:\n\n  | Local match? | Backend is `SyncProvider`? | Refresh outcome | Result |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | Yes | \u2014 | \u2014 | `DUPLICATE_FOUND` |\n  | No | No (SQLite/Memory/Beads) | not attempted | `NO_DUPLICATE` |\n  | No | Yes | succeeds, still no match | `NO_DUPLICATE` |\n  | No | Yes | succeeds, now matches | `DUPLICATE_FOUND` |\n  | No | Yes | raises `(GithubException, BacklogError)` | `COULD_NOT_VERIFY` (warning already appended to `out`) |\n\n- **`_check_for_duplicates`** \u2014 signature changes from\n  `(title: str, force: bool) -> None` to\n  `(title: str, description: str, force: bool, repo: str, out: Output) -> None`.\n  Thin wrapper around `_classify_duplicate_check`, dispatched with `match-case`\n  (Stage 1 review compliance \u2014 no `if/elif` chain on a discrete-value\n  variable):\n\n  ```python\n  def _check_for_duplicates(\n      title: str, description: str, force: bool, repo: str, out: Output\n  ) -> None:\n      if force:\n          return\n      status, matches = _classify_duplicate_check(title, description, repo, out)\n      match status:\n          case DuplicateCheckStatus.DUPLICATE_FOUND:\n              raise DuplicateItemError(matches)\n          case DuplicateCheckStatus.NO_DUPLICATE | DuplicateCheckStatus.COULD_NOT_VERIFY:\n              return\n  ```\n\n  `force=True` keeps meaning \"skip the check entirely\" (OQ-5 resolved: DO-3's\n  \"extend existing item\" path is a caller decision made *before* calling\n  `add_item` again with `force`, not a new value for this parameter).\n  `COULD_NOT_VERIFY` never raises \u2014 the warning was already attached to `out`\n  by `_classify_duplicate_check`, so `add_item` proceeds and the caller sees\n  the warning through the same `Output.warnings` channel both MCP and CLI\n  already surface (AC5: never a new rejection class).\n\n  Both functions stay **private** \u2014 nothing outside `add_item` needs to call\n  them directly. See \u00a74.4 for why no new *public* pre-check function is\n  introduced; `_classify_duplicate_check`'s return type is exactly what such a\n  function would expose unchanged, so this split costs nothing today and\n  removes the only real obstacle to adding one later.\n\n- **`add_item`** \u2014 call site changes from `_check_for_duplicates(title, force)`\n  to `_check_for_duplicates(title, description, force, repo, out)`. No other\n  change to `add_item`'s signature or contract.\n\n- **`list_items`** \u2014 new parameter `search: str | None = None`. After building\n  `result_items` (the existing `[_build_list_entry(it, status_map) for it in\n  open_items]` line), when `search` is not `None`, apply\n  `backlog_core.search.apply_search_filter(result_items, search)` before\n  building the returned dict. This is the single place both the CLI and the\n  MCP tool's non-`match_context` filtering now go through \u2014 `server.py`'s\n  `backlog_list` stops calling `_apply_search_filter` itself for the base\n  filter and instead lets `operations.list_items(search=search, ...)` do it;\n  `server.py` keeps its own `match_context` annotation layer on top of the\n  already-filtered result (match-context snippets are an MCP-presentation\n  concern, not a filtering concern \u2014 they stay in `server.py`, reading the\n  same `search.py` helpers).\n\n- **`find_fuzzy_duplicates`** (parsing.py) \u2014 removed. See ADR-004; nothing else\n  calls it (verified: only `_check_for_duplicates` and tests reference it).\n  `FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD` (models.py) removed with it.\n\n### 4.3 `backlog_core/models.py` (MODIFIED)\n\n- **`DuplicateItemError`** \u2014 redefined:\n\n  ```python\n  class DuplicateItemError(BacklogError):\n      \"\"\"Raised when one or more content-based duplicates are detected.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, duplicates: list[ContentDuplicateMatch]) -> None:\n          \"\"\"Initialize with the ranked list of ContentDuplicateMatch candidates.\"\"\"\n          ...\n  ```\n\n  Message format changes from `'\"{title}\" ({pct}%)'` to something built from\n  `item_ref` and `title` (e.g. `'\"{title}\" ({item_ref})'`) \u2014 percentage\n  similarity is meaningless for a token-match count and is dropped, not\n  re-derived as a fake percentage.\n\n- `find_fuzzy_duplicates` import removed from `operations.py`'s import block.\n\n### 4.4 Why no new public pre-check function\n\nThe dispatch brief asks for the check to be \"available as a standalone\npre-check callable before creation begins.\" That capability already exists and\nis unchanged by this spec: `backlog_list(search=..., match_context=true)` over\nMCP, which `create/start.md` Step 3 already calls. The only thing missing was\nCLI parity for that same call (\u00a74.5) \u2014 not a second operations.py-level\nfunction. Adding one anyway (e.g. `operations.check_for_content_duplicates()`\nreturning `DuplicateCheckResult` without raising) would be a second surface\nanswering the same question with no current caller \u2014 cut per YAGNI; add it if\na CLI subcommand or skill ever needs the tri-state result object directly\ninstead of a raw search-result list.\n\n### 4.5 `sam_schema/backlog.py` (MODIFIED \u2014 CLI)\n\n- **`list_items` command** \u2014 add:\n\n  ```python\n  search: Annotated[str | None, typer.Option(\"--search\", help=\"Full-text search query (see backlog_list search syntax)\")] = None,\n  ```\n\n  passed straight through as `operations.list_items(..., search=search, ...)`.\n  This mirrors the existing `merged_prs`'s `--search` option\n  (`sam_schema/backlog.py`, `~line 342`) verbatim \u2014 same option name, same\n  `str | None` type, same pass-through pattern.\n\n- **`add` command** \u2014 no signature change. `force` keeps its existing\n  `--force` help text (\"Force creation even if duplicate suspected\"); it is\n  unchanged by this spec.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Data Architecture\n\nNo new persisted schema. `ContentDuplicateMatch`/`DuplicateCheckStatus` are\ntransient, in-memory only \u2014 never written to backlog YAML, never serialized to\na file. They cross exactly one boundary: `operations.py` \u2192 the MCP/CLI error\nhandler that stringifies `BacklogError` (`str(exc)`), which already treats the\nexception message as opaque text (verified: no production code parses\n`.duplicates` or the message format outside tests \u2014 see \u00a79 concerns).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Type System Design\n\n### 6.1 Domain identifier inventory\n\n| Identifier | Values | Mechanism | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Duplicate-check outcome | 3, fixed | `StrEnum DuplicateCheckStatus` | Finite set, \u22653 wide, benefits from exhaustive `match-case` in the caller and IDE autocomplete \u2014 matches the StrEnum threshold in `type-system-design-patterns.md` \u00a72 |\n| Matched field label | open-ended (`\"title\"`, `\"body:acceptance-criteria\"`, \u2026) | Bare `str` | Already open-ended and produced by `_parse_body_sections`' slug derivation from arbitrary markdown headings \u2014 a closed enum would need updating every time a new section heading exists. Not a candidate for `NewType`/`StrEnum`; document as a deliberate exception (open vocabulary, not a fixed domain) |\n\n### 6.2 Type Contract: `ContentDuplicateMatch`\n\n- **Definition**: `@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True) class ContentDuplicateMatch` in `backlog_core/search.py`.\n- **Creation**: exclusively inside `find_content_duplicates()`; no other constructor call site.\n- **Validation**: none needed beyond the dataclass's own field types \u2014 all fields are derived from already-validated `BacklogItem`/list-entry data, not external input.\n- **Consumption**: `DuplicateItemError.__init__` (models.py); nothing else (\u00a79 concern: legacy `.duplicates` consumers are only tests, all updated per \u00a78).\n- **Serialisation**: not serialized directly. `DuplicateItemError`'s `str(exc)` message is the only externally visible projection, and it is plain text, not structured.\n- **Invariant**: `item_ref` is never empty and never a bare file path \u2014 it is always `item.issue` when set, else `item.reference` (the same actionable-handle precedence `add_item`'s own return dict already uses for `item_ref`/`reference`, see `operations.py` `add_item` docstring).\n\n### 6.3 Type Contract: `DuplicateCheckStatus`\n\n- **Definition**: `class DuplicateCheckStatus(StrEnum)` in `backlog_core/search.py`.\n- **Creation**: exactly one construction site \u2014 the return value of `operations._classify_duplicate_check()` (\u00a74.2). Not constructed by external callers in this iteration.\n- **Validation**: n/a \u2014 enum membership is enforced by the type checker.\n- **Consumption**: `operations._check_for_duplicates()`'s `match status:` dispatch (raise / return). Not currently returned across a public boundary; kept as a named enum rather than encoding the three outcomes as booleans/exceptions because a future public pre-check (\u00a74.4) would return `_classify_duplicate_check`'s result type unchanged.\n- **Serialisation**: n/a (never crosses a serialization boundary in this iteration).\n- **Invariant**: `COULD_NOT_VERIFY` is only ever produced when a `SyncProvider` refresh attempt raised \u2014 never produced for native-storage backends (SQLite/Memory/Beads), which have no staleness class to report.\n\n### 6.4 Weak-type audit\n\n- `list[dict[str, str | bool]]` for search candidates: **not** replaced with a\n  `TypedDict`. This shape is inherited from the pre-existing\n  `_build_list_entry` return type (already used identically by `backlog_list`\n  today); introducing a `TypedDict` here is a larger, unrelated refactor of a\n  function this item does not otherwise touch. Flagged, not fixed \u2014 see \u00a79\n  concerns.\n- No `Any`, no `cast()`, no bare `object` introduced by this spec.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Security Architecture\n\nNo new attack surface. `build_concept_query`'s stopword/tokenization is pure\nstring processing over already-validated `title`/`description` fields (already\npast the CLI/MCP boundary's own validation, per `_validate_add_item_priority`\net al.). No subprocess, no new file I/O, no new network endpoint \u2014 the\nincremental-refresh call in \u00a74.2 step 4 is the *existing*\n`refresh_local_cache_from_github` function, calling the *existing* GitHub\nclient through the *existing* auth path; this spec does not touch credential\nhandling.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Testing Architecture\n\nStack unchanged: `pytest`, `pytest-mock` (`MockerFixture`), no `unittest.mock`.\n\n### 8.1 Tests that must be rewritten (breaking, expected)\n\n- **`tests/test_backlog_core_parsing.py::TestFindFuzzyDuplicates`** (~14 tests)\n  and **`TestFindFuzzyDuplicatesEdgeCases`** \u2014 deleted along with\n  `find_fuzzy_duplicates`. Replaced by a new\n  `tests/test_backlog_core_search.py::TestFindContentDuplicates` covering the\n  same edge-case shapes (exact match, dissimilar, skip-flagged items, empty\n  title/description, custom `max_results`) **plus** the item's own failing\n  pair from the incident report (\"CI check for drift\u2026\" vs \"Agent `tools:`\n  frontmatter drifts\u2026\") as a required regression case \u2014 the one input the old\n  suite could never express because it never matched.\n- **`tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py::TestAddItemDuplicateDetection`**\n  (~3 tests) \u2014 updated to pass `description` in fixtures and to assert against\n  `ContentDuplicateMatch` shapes, not `(title, ratio, path)` tuples. Timing\n  assertions (`add_item` still raises synchronously) are unchanged since the\n  gate stays inside `add_item`.\n- **`tests/test_backlog_core_models.py::TestDuplicateItemError`** (~7 tests) \u2014\n  rewritten against `list[ContentDuplicateMatch]` input and the new message\n  format. Confirmed breaking, confirmed expected (per dispatch brief).\n\n### 8.2 New tests required (previously-identified gaps, per codebase-testing analysis)\n\n- `TestCheckForDuplicatesFreshness` (new, in `test_backlog_core_operations.py`):\n  - `SyncProvider` backend, no local match, refresh succeeds with a new match \u2192\n    raises `DuplicateItemError` (the concurrent-session case).\n  - `SyncProvider` backend, no local match, refresh raises `GithubException` \u2192\n    `add_item` succeeds AND `output.warnings` contains one entry \u2014 this is the\n    behavioral proof for AC5 + DO-2 together in one test.\n  - Non-`SyncProvider` backend (Memory) \u2192 refresh is never attempted (assert\n    via `mocker.patch` on `refresh_local_cache_from_github` with\n    `assert_not_called()`).\n- `TestListItemsSearch` (new, in operations tests) and\n  `TestBacklogListCliSearch` (new, in `sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py`):\n  same query against both the CLI and MCP path returns the same item set \u2014\n  the concrete DO-7/AC4 regression test for \"MCP and CLI equivalence.\"\n- DO-5 measurement (OQ-8 resolved): add a fixed corpus of ~10 known\n  non-duplicate pairs drawn from real, resolved, unrelated backlog items\n  (same subsystem, deliberately dissimilar problem) to\n  `TestFindContentDuplicates` as a parametrized \"must NOT match\" table. This\n  is the regression gate for \"no increase in false positives\" \u2014 a judgement\n  call converted into a pinned fixture, not left as a manual review step.\n\n### 8.3 Coverage target\n\nStandard project target (80% line/branch) applies; `find_content_duplicates`\nand `_check_for_duplicates`'s three-branch freshness logic are business logic,\nnot critical-path (no payment/auth/security surface), so the 95%+/mutation-testing\nbar does not apply \u2014 flagged and explicitly not over-specified.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Distribution Architecture\n\nNot applicable \u2014 no new package, no new entry point, no PEP 723 script. All\nchanges land inside the existing `backlog_core`/`sam_schema` packages under\ntheir current build configuration.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Architectural Decisions\n\n| ADR | Decision | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| ADR-001 | New module `backlog_core/search.py`, not `parsing.py` | `parsing.py`'s existing responsibility is markdown/frontmatter parsing; the search engine (~250 lines: tokenizer, recursive-descent parser, predicate AST, snippet formatting) is a distinct concern that would roughly double that file's size. A new module also gives the primitive a name (`search`) that matches the MCP tool it powers (`backlog_list(search=...)`), making the shared-primitive relationship legible from the import alone. |\n| ADR-002 | Duplicate check stays inside `add_item`; no new gate is introduced elsewhere | AC5 requires no new false-positive class, and moving the check out of `add_item` would remove the CLI's last-line-of-defense role for scripted/dispatch callers per AC4. The pre-write advisory path already exists (`backlog_list(search=...)`) \u2014 this item makes it CLI-reachable, it does not duplicate it as a second write-time gate. |\n| ADR-003 | Freshness verification is refresh-on-empty-result, not refresh-always | Refreshing on every `add_item` call regresses the common case (R-2) and add_item is called in loops by dispatch/scripting contexts. Refreshing only when about to declare \"no duplicate\" pays the network cost exactly once, only on the path where correctness is being asserted, and only for the one backend type (`SyncProvider`/GitHub) that has a staleness class at all. |\n| ADR-004 | `find_fuzzy_duplicates`/`difflib.SequenceMatcher` removed, not kept as a fallback | Token-overlap matching over full content is the established approach for this class of problem (title+body duplicate/near-duplicate detection on short records) \u2014 character-sequence edit distance is documented in the literature as weak specifically against reordering and differently-worded-but-topically-identical text, which is exactly the incident's failure mode. Keeping both as parallel paths would violate \"one shared primitive\" (problem 1) and reintroduce the exact bifurcation this item exists to close (R-8: partial fix looks like a fix). See brief web research: token-overlap/set-based similarity is preferred over edit distance for exactly this failure mode (word reordering, abbreviation, non-identical phrasing) \u2014 [Wikiversity: Duplicate record detection](https://en.wikiversity.org/wiki/Duplicate_record_detection); character edit-distance is noted as weak against reordering/truncation (\"does not work well when matching strings that have been truncated, or shortened\") \u2014 [Deep Dive into String Similarity](https://dev.to/ademakdogan/deep-dive-into-string-similarity-from-edit-distance-to-fuzzy-matching-theory-and-practice-in-python-4hnf). |\n| ADR-005 | `DuplicateItemError` shape change is a breaking change, not a compatibility shim | No production consumer parses `.duplicates` or the message text today (verified by repo-wide grep \u2014 only tests reference either). A compatibility union type (`list[tuple] | list[ContentDuplicateMatch]`) would keep two shapes alive for zero real callers \u2014 cut per YAGNI. |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Scalability Strategy\n\n- The candidate list read (`backend.list_work_items()`) is unchanged in size\n  and frequency from today \u2014 same O(items) cache read, once per `add_item`\n  call (plus one conditional incremental refresh, bounded by GitHub's own\n  delta window, only on the no-match path for `SyncProvider` backends).\n- `find_content_duplicates` reuses `apply_search_filter`, which is already the\n  production filter for `backlog_list` at current backlog sizes (hundreds of\n  items) \u2014 no new performance class is introduced.\n- No async change: `_check_for_duplicates` stays synchronous, called from the\n  already-synchronous `add_item`; the MCP tool already wraps `add_item` in\n  `asyncio.to_thread`, unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Documentation Migration (implementation moves to match docs, not the reverse)\n\nPer the dispatch brief: `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` and `create/start.md`\nStep 3 already describe search-based detection. This spec makes the\nimplementation match them, not the other way round. Docs that must be updated\nonce implemented:\n\n- **`docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`** (lines ~126, 154, 177 per the\n  codebase-patterns analysis) \u2014 currently internally ambiguous about whether\n  Step 3 is content-scoped or title-scoped (flagged as a verification finding\n  in the feature-context artifact, \u00a78). Resolve the ambiguity explicitly:\n  content-scoped, token/boolean matching (not semantic), matching\n  `create/start.md`.\n- **`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md`** Step 3 \u2014\n  no behavior change needed (it already specifies the target design), but add\n  one line noting the CLI can now perform the same check via\n  `backlog list --search` for scripted/dispatch contexts that cannot call MCP.\n- **`skills/backlog/SKILL.md`** \u2014 any reference to \"fuzzy\"/\"0.85 threshold\" (or\n  the 0.80 constant used elsewhere) must be removed; this spec deletes\n  `FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD` entirely. Grep this file for the literal\n  strings `fuzzy` and `0.8` before closing the item.\n- **Generated workflow-graph mirrors**: `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` and the\n  `workflow-layers/L1-trace-work-backlog-item.json` /\n  `workflow-layers/G8-backend-routing.json` layers mirror Step 3 and the\n  backend-routing behavior. These are generated artifacts \u2014 run\n  `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh` after implementation, do not hand-edit them.\n- **`backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md`** \u2014 no change needed; this spec brings the\n  duplicate-check code into compliance with the invariant already stated there\n  (line ~436), it does not change the invariant.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Acceptance-Criteria Traceability\n\n| AC / DO | Satisfied by |\n|---|---|\n| DO-1 (content match, not title chars) | \u00a74.1 `find_content_duplicates` + `apply_search_filter` over `body` (full description + section content) |\n| DO-2 (detect-or-disclose, never silent stale \"no duplicate\") | \u00a74.2 step 4 \u2014 tri-state internal to `_check_for_duplicates`; COULD_NOT_VERIFY \u2192 warning, never silent success |\n| DO-3 (actionable reference + content) | \u00a74.1 `ContentDuplicateMatch.item_ref` + `.snippet`; \u00a74.3 `DuplicateItemError` redefinition |\n| DO-4 (CLI path produces a result) | \u00a74.5 CLI `--search`; write-time gate already ran on the CLI `add` path before this item and continues to |\n| DO-5 (no false-positive increase) | \u00a78.2 pinned non-duplicate corpus test; \u00a74.1 ranking by `match_count` rather than a single scalar threshold avoids the 0.80-cliff behavior that produced no false positives *or* true positives correctly before |\n| DO-6 (timing \u2014 before effort spent) | \u00a74.4 \u2014 pre-write path already exists via `backlog_list(search=...)`; unchanged, now CLI-reachable |\n| DO-7 (MCP/CLI equivalence) | \u00a74.5 + \u00a78.2 `TestBacklogListCliSearch` cross-interface regression test |\n"}